-- 013_generation_2025_backfill.sql
-- Date: 2026-07-06
-- Description: 2025 annual generation backfill from IAEA PRIS Operating History tables
--   (Electricity Supplied[GW.h]), plus 2024 gap-fills that PRIS has since reported.
--   PRIS pages fetched 2026-07-06 via curl (browser UA, ~1 req/s). electricity_gwh only
--   (capacity_factor/availability_factor are computed on the fly by app.py and were NULL
--   for all recent rows). INSERT OR IGNORE so any pre-existing (reactor,year) is untouched.
-- Rows: 399 new 2025 + 11 new 2024 = 410. Affected table: generation_annual.
--   (5 units PRIS-reported 0 GWh for 2025 (extended outage/refurb: Atucha-1, Bruce-3,
--    Darlington-4, Kori-2, Kori-3) were EXCLUDED — the DB represents idle years by absence, not 0-rows.
-- Sampling (12 reactors, spread) hand-verified against their PRIS pages — see cooling_audit /
--   migration report. CF sanity: 21 rows compute >102% vs net reference power; all are
--   high-performing units under gross nameplate EXCEPT Sendai-2 (2025 PRIS value slightly
--   exceeds the DB's conservative gross figure). No rows deleted/altered — PRIS values mirrored.
--
-- CORRECTION (2026-07-06, pre-commit, spec-blind review finding): the CF-sanity note above
--   was wrong — several of those flags were NOT gross-vs-net artifacts but real corruption
--   (up to 238% CF on permanently-shutdown reactors). This migration keyed pages by
--   reactors.pris_id, and 13 reactors carried ANOTHER reactor's pris_id (pre-existing bug),
--   so both members of each duplicate-id pair received the id-owner's output; 9 of the 11
--   "2024 gap-fills" and 10 of the 2025 rows landed on the wrong reactor. REPAIRED IN
--   MIGRATION 015 (ids fixed from a full PRIS id-space scan; bad rows deleted/corrected from
--   each reactor's true page). Validator checks 12-14 now make this class impossible to ship.

